  "scope": "# Review \u2014 537b409b6744 candidate-rank prototype\n\n- Assignment: `review-69cf4b6df84bd4f6`; selected generator SHA-256 `61fe1c7026345bbfe8521c5b41576a8bda5a4695d037b84b255eb75461baa3ab`.\n- Status: **proposed task-local prototype**; production generator, canonical ledger, approval, and training status are unchanged.\n- Missing extension repaired: one episode-wide `candidate_rank` parameter with values `nearest` (canonical/default) and `farthest` (proposed).\n- `nearest.rkt` is byte-identical to canonical; `farthest.rkt` reverses only primary gap order and preserves the larger-wall tie-break.\n- Each retained episode has 3 demonstrations and 4 distinct queries under one fixed setting.\n- Real Racket labeled 14/14 episode pairs; the independent Python mirror matched 14/14.\n- Both lessons are demo-identifiable; 8/8 retained queries change under the rival; 14/14 leave-one-out rotations retain a refuting demonstration.\n- Canonical/default replay remains 8/8; production `generator.py` was not edited.\n- Public files omit hidden state and answers and are named by SHA-256 of their exact visible bytes, not setting, seed, or ordinal.\n- Focused and adversarial checks pass on equal-gap tie parity, stale-rule rejection, metadata/output leaks, boolean cells, duplicate visible payloads, and private/public path separation.",
